@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] backup-runtime-custody
Passwords and connection strings MUST come from private runtime credentials,
never Nix values, argv, status, manifests or diagnostics. Only fixed executables
and validated argument arrays may execute; secret environment files are never
sourced as shell programs.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] backup-completion-and-cleanup
A complete host recovery point MUST reference successful captures of every
required component. Flush failure or a stopped guest MUST NOT exclude its disks.
Every owned snapshot MUST have durable cleanup intent before creation; uncertain
cleanup remains visible and retryable. Foreign snapshots MUST never be destroyed.
A published complete manifest MUST pass its own retention validator, including
when the wall clock steps backward between started_at and publication.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] backup-retention-reachability
Retention MUST preserve all component snapshots referenced by retained completed
host manifests. Failed runs MUST NOT advance successful retention or erase the
last good recovery points. All repository mutations MUST share the host lock.
